-- title:
--   Kernel-ideal transport along a Hecke idele at q
-- statement:
--   Let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic a prime $q'$, algebraic over $\mathbb{F}_{q'}$, and let $X_1/\kappa$ be an elliptic Weierstrass curve whose only $q'$-torsion point is $0$. Let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ satisfy $a<0$, $b<0$ and the condition that, for a height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$, the algebra $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v$ is a division algebra exactly when $q'\in v$; let $\Lambda_1$ be a maximal order (an order contained in no strictly larger order) of $\mathbb{H}=\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$, and $\theta_1$ an injective ring homomorphism from the subring of $\operatorname{End}(X_1(\kappa))$ generated by the rational homomorphisms $X_1\to X_1$ onto $\Lambda_1$. Fix $N\neq 0$ with $q'\nmid N$ and a unit $m$ of $\mathbb{H}\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\widehat{\mathbb{Q}}$ (finite adeles) lying in the adelic box $\widehat{\Lambda_1}$ with $N\,m^{-1}\in\widehat{\Lambda_1}$ and $m\widehat{\Lambda_1}m^{-1}\cap\mathbb{H}$ maximal, such that $R=\Lambda_1\cap m\widehat{\Lambda_1}m^{-1}$ has relative index $N$ in $\Lambda_1$. Fix a prime $q$ with $q\nmid N$ and $q'\nmid Nq$, and likewise $m'$ with $m'\in\widehat{\Lambda_1}$, $Nq\,m'^{-1}\in\widehat{\Lambda_1}$, conjugate order maximal, and $S=\Lambda_1\cap m'\widehat{\Lambda_1}m'^{-1}$ of relative index $Nq$ in $\Lambda_1$. Let $n$ belong to the Hecke set of $R$ at $q$, i.e. $n\in\widehat{R}$, $q\,n^{-1}\in\widehat{R}$, $n^{-1}\notin\widehat{R}$, $q^{-1}n\notin\widehat{R}$, and assume $S=R\cap n\widehat{R}n^{-1}$ and $n\widehat{S}n^{-1}=\widehat{S}$. Let $x$ be a further finite idele and $d\in\mathbb{H}^{\times}$. Assume given: an elliptic $W$ and a non-zero rational homomorphism $\chi:X_1\to W$ with $\theta_1$ of the set of rational composites $\rho\circ\chi$, $\rho\in\operatorname{Hom}(W,X_1)$, equal to the quaternion conjugate of $d\cdot(\mathbb{H}\cap x\widehat{\Lambda_1})$; an elliptic $W'$ and rational $\psi:W\to W'$, $\psi':W'\to W$ with $\psi'\circ\psi=\psi\circ\psi'=[Nq]$, such that the analogous kernel-ideal image for $\psi\circ\chi$ is the conjugate of $d\cdot(\mathbb{H}\cap xm'\widehat{\Lambda_1})$, with $\ker\psi$ cyclic of order $Nq$; a point $Q\in\ker\psi$ of order $q$; and an elliptic $V$ with rational $\pi:W\to V$ whose kernel is $\langle Q\rangle$ and which is universal among rational homomorphisms out of $W$ killing $Q$ (every such $\alpha$ factors as a rational $\gamma$ composed after $\pi$). Then $\pi\circ\chi\neq 0$, the kernel-ideal image of $\pi\circ\chi$ is the conjugate of $d\cdot(\mathbb{H}\cap xn\widehat{\Lambda_1})$, and there exist an elliptic $V'$ and rational $\rho:V\to V'$, $\rho':V'\to V$ with $\rho'\circ\rho=\rho\circ\rho'=[Nq]$, the kernel-ideal image of $\rho\circ\pi\circ\chi$ equal to the conjugate of $d\cdot(\mathbb{H}\cap xnm'\widehat{\Lambda_1})$, and $\ker\rho=\pi(\ker\psi+W[q])$, cyclic of order $Nq$.
--
--   This is the Deuring-type dictionary step transporting a kernel-ideal realisation of a finite idele $x$ at level $Nq$ to one of $xn$, where $n$ is a Hecke element at $q$ normalising the Eichler-type order $S$: the new realisation is obtained by dividing $W$ by the order-$q$ part of its cyclic level structure, and the resulting level structure is the Atkin–Lehner transform $\pi(\ker\psi+W[q])$. It feeds the identification of the Atkin–Lehner action on supersingular places in the Čerednik–Drinfeld comparison, being cited by [`CerednikDrinfeld.autOnPlaces_eq_of_isAtkinLehnerLevelAut_of_forall_toValuationSubring_eq_comap_moduliPlace`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.autOnPlaces_eq_of_isAtkinLehnerLevelAut_of_forall_toValuationSubring_eq_comap_moduliPlace).
